<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francia was the realm of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, covering much of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It formed the heart of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>, and its forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> halted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>'s advance at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tours">Battle of Tours</a> in 732.</p></div>
